{
  "id": "MP-CHANGE-2026-0713-007",
  "title": "Harden CSV rerun lifecycle and source recovery",
  "version_target": "2026.06.04.001",
  "status": "complete",
  "type": "bugfix",
  "risk_level": "high",
  "date_started": "2026-07-13",
  "date_completed": "2026-07-14",
  "summary": "Make dedicated local and Network CSV rerun lifecycle evidence durable, visible beside the normal queue, explicit in the WebView, and recoverable across temporary source outages.",
  "reason": "Confirmed acceptance-to-manifest evidence gaps, fallback-only queue projection, ambiguous spawned-versus-running UI language, missing source outage classification, and stranded Network retry/reclaim states matched the reported operator symptoms.",
  "affected_areas": [
    "backend",
    "contracts",
    "desktop",
    "documentation",
    "generated-context",
    "network",
    "pipeline",
    "queue",
    "rerun-lifecycle",
    "tauri",
    "tests",
    "validation",
    "webview"
  ],
  "behavior_before": "Local CSV reruns could spawn before a durable command/batch/launch/enrollment/manifest correlation chain existed, leaving early exits or interrupted spawn transitions ambiguous. Dedicated rerun work was projected into Queue only as a fallback and stale progress could revive terminal history. Source recovery did not distinguish an unavailable configured root from a missing leaf, access failure, or changed identity, and lacked an authoritative pre-outage full-content hash. Network retry/release/done transitions had stale-claim and compare-and-set gaps, destination work could execute while holding batch-state authority, and exhausted or waiting rows lacked a strict idempotent recovery route. Close-readiness treated safe durable waiting-only Network state as active while not explicitly blocking ambiguous local rerun exits. The WebView reported accepted reruns as started and inferred continuation behavior instead of rendering backend-authored actions and evidence.",
  "behavior_after": "Local reruns are durably enrolled before spawn with one command, batch, launch, ActiveJobs, enrollment, and execution-manifest correlation chain; child exit and backend startup reconcile that evidence without replay, while ambiguous exits fail closed and block close-readiness. Queue combines normal rows with dedicated rerun rows, uses evidence recency and authority to suppress stale terminal progress, and exposes explicit source/count/correlation fields. Bounded source probes classify unavailable roots, missing leaves, access failures, and identity changes separately; recovery requires an authoritative full-file SHA-256 captured before outage and materializes exactly-once recovery CSVs with request IDs. Network claim/release/done paths use locked compare-and-set transitions, bounded retry/backoff/exhaustion, strict manual retry confirmation, stale-claim protection, and review-only handling for ambiguous output or interrupted destination policy. Durable waiting-only Network state becomes close-safe only after coordinator shutdown. The WebView refreshes rerun evidence, renders backend-authored actions, timelines, and Network-only counts, and labels accepted reruns accurately.",
